WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.734
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.734
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:08.467
You're watching. Thank you.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.634
Well, guys,
the big story continues to be

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:13.434
the FBI's search of former
president Trump's home

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.033
at Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.734
Seriously, you know
you did something bad when

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:18.734
you're the former president
but you're still making

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:22.100
more headlines than the current
president, don't you think?

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.467
You've got to hand it
to Trump, though.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.701
He has endless scandals
for six years

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:28.133
and he always manages to keep
them feeling fresh and new,

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.901
don't you think?

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.200
Yeah, the action never stops.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.133
It's like if Discovery
ran Shark Week

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.300
24 hours a day, 365 days a year.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.801
That's what this is.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.467
Well, over the weekend,
we found out that the FBI seized

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:42.300
11 sets of classified documents
from Trump's home,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.434
including four sets
that were marked "top secret."

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.334
[ AUDIENCE "Oohs" ]

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.200
You know Trump just kept those
hoping to come across

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.334
KFC's secret blend
of herbs and spices.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:55.801
He's like, "I've got something
on the Colonel."

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.400
Also, just a thought,
but if the government

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.167
doesn't want
people reading those files,

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.200
maybe they shouldn't label them
"top secret."

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.234
It's like a guy labeling a porn
folder on his computer

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.467
"Best Porn."

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:13.100
It's like, just call it
"banana-bread recipe."

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.834
No one will open that.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.367
This doesn't
look good for Trump.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:19.534
But don't worry.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.100
He had a perfectly
reasonable explanation.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.033
He said that when he took
the classified documents

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:26.601
from The White House,
he declassified them.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.968
Yeah. He declassified them,
meaning he took out a Sharpie

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.467
and wrote "D-E"
in front of "classified."

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:37.000
"They are
officially declassified.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.400
Get the Colonel on the phone."

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.334
I read that,
after the FBI search last week,

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.767
Trump sent a message to
Attorney General Merrick Garland

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.834
that said,
"The country is on fire.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:48.033
What can I do
to reduce the heat?"

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.167
Garland was like, "I don't know,

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.467
but why are you talking like
a 1950s private eye?

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:57.834
It's like, "I need to
find those nuclear codes, see?

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.300
What's going on, see?"

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.734
Meanwhile, today,
Trump complained

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:03.167
that during their
search of Mar-a-Lago,

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:06.067
the FBI seized
his three passports.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.300
He's like, "What's next?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.434
They take my fake beard

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:11.367
and emergency bag of
getaway money?"

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:12.934
Switching gears.
Did you guys see this?

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:15.801
Senator Chuck Grassley, who is
88 years old, by the way,

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.701
is running for
re-election in Iowa.

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.801
And he just put out
a campaign video

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:19.801
to show that he's still got it.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:20.801
Take a look at this.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:21.968
-I get up at 4:00.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.400
I run a couple miles.
That's my habit.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.100
I started running
when I was 65 years old.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.100
-Wow.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.267
I think people are like,
"Hey, honey, honey,

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.701
you know that 88-year-old
who runs around the

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:37.167
neighborhood at 4:00 a.m.,
in the miner's cap?

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.367
Apparently, that's our Senator."

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.501
He also wears that head lamp to
read menus in restaurants.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.701
I've seen it.

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:47.801
Well, this is good.

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.934
A Canadian politician
named Doug Ford

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:52.300
was giving a speech when
he was interrupted by a bee.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.701
Check this out.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:57.267
-Not coming from the --
not coming from the government,

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:58.667
per se, the premier.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:00.501
It's coming from
the health sector.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.868
[ Coughs ]

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:05.100
Holy Christ.
I just swallowed a bee.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.701
Holy Christ.
I need a little...

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.734
-And right now,
that is the biggest

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:12.133
political scandal in Canada.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.734
Right now. That.

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:17.534
That is the biggest...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.634
Guys, it is the beginning
of the week,

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.968
and I thought it would be nice
to kick things off

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.601
with a few words
of encouragement.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:27.501
It's time for some
"Monday Motivations."

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:31.934
-♪ Monday motivations ♪

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:34.601
♪♪

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.067
-Hey.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:38.400
You look normal when you run.

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:43.133
That houseplant died of old age.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:45.334
There was nothing you could do.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.567
When you order a pizza,
the guy on the phone is like,

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.300
"Dang, I never thought of
that topping combo,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.400
but it sounds amazing."

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.167
Your dad says
he's proud of you all the time.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.868
You're just never
in the room when he's saying it.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:03.501
Of course you're
pulling off the hat.

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.868
You're a total hat guy.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.501
When you go into a store,

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:11.267
the mannequins want to buy
what you're wearing.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:15.300
That can you just recycled?

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.334
That's the one
that saves the Earth.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:24.067
Just a little Monday motivation.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.634
Am I?
-Hey, you're a hat guy.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:31.400
-Oh, you're totally pulling --
A fedora? Yes.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.667
Some business news.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:35.234
I saw that Uber Eats
teamed up with Office Depot

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:38.467
to offer on-demand delivery
of office and school supplies.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.501
Yeah. They even have
a cool name for it --

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.400
Amazon.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.734
You know that
excited feeling you get

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.467
when your Uber Eats
order shows up?

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:47.767
Yeah, this won't be like that.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.734
It's like, "Honey,
our ink cartridges are here."

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:51.934
Well, get this.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:53.934
Apparently, this year's
brands and companies

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:56.000
are rolling out
their pumpkin-spice offerings

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.567
earlier than ever before.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:05:01.367
[ Crowd cheers ]
I feel like it's too soon.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.701
I mean, even though I do --
I do love pumpkin spice.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:06.133
-Oh, really?
You like pumpkin spice?

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.300
What else?

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.567
-What else?

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:12.100
I like pumpkin spice.
I like orange Slice.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.267
-That's cool. What else?

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:17.634
-I like yellow rice
and Disney on Ice.

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.968
I like wearing half-priced
Old Spice in tights,

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.801
while singing "Edelweiss"
with D-Nice.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.467
I like watching Vice,
"Bachelor in Paradise,"

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:24.868
and picking lice off mice

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:26.968
with Willie Geist
and Condoleezza Rice.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.834
Oh, did I say "rice" twice?
Nice.

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:31.334
I like my coffee ice,
Creed "Sacrifice,"

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:32.400
getting concise advice from

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.200
"The Price is Right" and
"In the Heights."

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:46.467
-Quest, how do you feel
about pumpkin spice?

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:48.501
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.701
No dice.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.234
-Moving on.
Hey, guys, listen to this.

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:58.400
I heard that,
due to weak tomato production,

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.601
there could be a shortage of

00:05:59.601 --> 00:06:02.834
spaghetti sauce,
ketchup, and salsa.

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:04.200
It's getting pretty bad.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.267
Levels of concern
have gone from mild to medium.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.067
I knew there was
a tomato shortage

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.400
when, after they
raided Mar-a-Lago,

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.601
Trump threw mustard at the wall
instead of ketchup.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:15.267
Well, this is big.

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:17.834
The CDC has ended most of
its recommendations

00:06:17.834 --> 00:06:19.234
for social distancing,

00:06:19.234 --> 00:06:21.734
quarantining,
and contact tracing.

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.367
Yeah, they got rid of --
Now they're replacing them

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:25.167
with some new COVID guidelines.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:29.300
First of all, all hand sanitizer
is now illegal.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.567
Next...

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:35.234
Next up...

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:39.734
Next...

00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:41.734
Then there's...

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:46.434
[ Crowd chanting "Lick it!" ]

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:52.868
Then...

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.367
And finally...

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:59.567
That's on the CDC...

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:02.434
"Lick it." Oh, my gosh.
Thank you.

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:05.667
Well, this is going viral.

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:08.267
An athlete in Estonia decided to
propose to his girlfriend

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:10.501
at the finish line
of an Ironman.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.601
-Oh.

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:13.801
-But his muscles
had a different plan.

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:15.000
Take a look at this.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.701
-We want to tell his story,

00:07:16.701 --> 00:07:19.267
and we think
he wants to say something.

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:33.701
-Come on, buddy. Come on.

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:36.033
-Will you marry me?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:42.234
[ Sad tuba plays ]
-Oh!

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.033
-You know your proposal
went wrong

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:49.133
when it looks like
you're being tased, you know?

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:50.701
That's how she always
dreamt about it --

00:07:50.701 --> 00:07:52.501
getting proposed to
by her boyfriend

00:07:52.501 --> 00:07:54.934
while two guys
rubbed his hamstrings.

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:04.133
And, finally,
Snoop Dogg just launched

00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:09.000
his very first breakfast cereal,
called Snoop Loopz.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.267
They look pretty good.
They even got marshmallows.

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:12.801
But he's not the only rapper

00:08:12.801 --> 00:08:14.567
launching his
own breakfast cereal, no.

00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:15.834
-Really?
-Yeah, there's also...

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:19.300
Next, there's...

00:08:20.868 --> 00:08:23.467
And, finally, of course...

00:08:23.467 --> 00:08:25.133
There you go.
We have a great show.

